        <item>
            <title>2.10.4</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 18:13:25 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>79</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.10.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Changes
- The context meter now takes its colour from the CLI's own warn / compact / blocked levels instead of round percentage cutoffs. Past the limit it adds a warning icon, and the tooltip names the state in words — whether auto-compact is merely due, or the next request will be refused outright.
- The context percentage is no longer clamped at 100%, so the distance between "compaction is due" and "requests are refused" stays visible instead of flattening into a single 100%.
- Updated Sparkle to 2.9.4, which includes hardening on the delta-update path Canopy uses for smaller downloads.

### Bug Fixes
- Fixed the context meter reading far too optimistically when a subagent ran on a model with a wider context window than the main model. A 200K session with one 1M subagent could show roughly 17% while the context was in fact full.
- Fixed the context meter reaching 100% early on models whose maximum output budget exceeds the CLI's internal reserve cap, which made sessions look nearly exhausted long before they were.
]]></description>
